-- title:
--   p-saturation of global differentials via q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero $N$, a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$, a ring embedding $\iota_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ into $\mathbb C$, and let $R$ be [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb Q$ of fractions whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ with $X$ integral, and let $\mathcal V$ be a cover of $X$ by two affine opens $U_0,U_1$ with affine intersection; write $H$ for the group `(𝒱.kaehlerSections c).H0`, the kernel of $(\omega_0,\omega_1)\mapsto \omega_1|_{U_0\cap U_1}-\omega_0|_{U_0\cap U_1}$ on $\Omega_{\Gamma(X,U_0)/R}\times\Omega_{\Gamma(X,U_1)/R}$. The hypotheses supply: a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbb Q$ of the field $F_N\subset\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the expansions $j(q^d)$, $d\mid N$, an isomorphism $e_0$ of $M_0.C$ with the $\mathbb Q$-fibre of $c$ over the structure morphisms, whose generic point lies in the chart $U_0$; a ring map $\iota$ from $\Gamma(X,U_0)$ to $\bar F_N=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` sending a section to the $q$-expansion of its germ at the generic point, compatible with $R\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and the additive map `res` on $H$ obtained by transporting the first component along $(R\to\overline{\mathbb Q},\iota)$; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$ and a $\mathbb Q$-point $y$ of the fibre lying over $\varepsilon_\infty$ and hitting a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose place is the cusp $\infty$; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\bar F_N$ identified with the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-fibre of $c$, whose point–place bijection is Galois-equivariant for the coefficientwise action and whose places restrict along $F_N\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}\otimes_{\mathbb Q}F_N\cong\bar F_N$ to the places of the matching closed points of $M_0.C$; and, for each valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $p$ is a nonunit, a lift $\rho$ of $R\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to $A$, a curve model $M_A$ over the residue field of $A$ of the corresponding field of $q$-expansions identified with the fibre of $c$, and (when that residue field is algebraically closed) a degree-preserving, divisor-compatible reduction map $r$ on places matching the point–place bijections of $M_\eta$ and $M_A$ along $A$-points of $X$. Under all this, if $\omega\in H$ and $P\in R[[q]]$ satisfy that the $q$-expansion `diffQExpBar N (res ω)` equals the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ attached to the image of $p\cdot P$, then $\omega=p\,\omega'$ for some $\omega'\in H$.
--
--   This is the $p$-saturation statement for the module of global relative differentials on the smooth proper $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$-model of the modular curve of level $N$ with $p \nmid N$: a global differential whose $q$-expansion at the cusp $\infty$ is divisible by $p$ is itself $p$ times a global differential. It is used to identify the integral lattice of $q$-expansions in [`ModularCurve.exists_kaehlerH0_coeffMap_diffQExpBar_eq_qExpansion_of_mem_intLattice_of_ratCurveModel_of_cuspSection_compat_of_neZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_kaehlerH0_coeffMap_diffQExpBar_eq_qExpansion_of_mem_intLattice_of_ratCurveModel_of_cuspSection_compat_of_neZero).
-- source:
